>> title: Paella
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, chicken, shrimp, saffron, spanish, one-pot
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: paella mixta, Spanish rice pan, paella de carne y marisco, arroz en paella
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — nothing is stirred once the stock goes in, and the socarrat at the bottom is heard rather than seen: a faint crackle in the last two minutes and the pan comes off. Past that it is burnt rice, and a paella that was stirred is a good rice dish and not this
>> step.1: One wide shallow pan, and the rice is spread in it in a layer no deeper than a thumbnail so every grain sits in liquid rather than in other rice. From the moment the stock goes in, nothing is stirred again. A paella that is stirred is a rice dish, and a good one, but it is not this.
>> step.2: brown 10 min
>> step.3: sweat the sofrito 8 min
>> step.4: toast the rice 2 min, spread it flat
>> step.5: boil hard 10 min, do not stir
>> step.6: simmer low 8 min, shrimp on top
>> step.7: rest 10 min under a towel
>> step.8: The crust on the bottom is the point and it is the one thing a table cannot hand you: it comes from a pan that is hotter at the edges than the middle, and only your own burner knows that. Listen for it in the last two minutes — a faint crackle, not a smell of burning — and pull the pan when you hear it.

One wide shallow pan, and the rice is spread in it in a layer no deeper than a thumbnail so every grain sits in liquid rather than in other rice. From the moment the stock goes in, nothing is stirred again. A paella that is stirred is a rice dish, and a good one, but it is not this.

Brown @bone-in chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; cut in 2-in pieces), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @olive oil{3%Tbs} in a #paella pan{} for ~brown{10%min}.

Soften @&(~1)browned chicken{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @plum tomatoes{3}(grated), @sweet paprika{2%tsp} for ~saute{8%min}.

Toast @&(~1)sofrito{} with @bomba rice{2%cups}(400 g), @saffron{1/2%tsp}(crumbled), @flat green beans{6%oz}(170 g; cut in 2-in lengths) for ~toast{2%min}.

Boil @&(~1)rice{} hard with @chicken stock{5%cups}(1.2 L; hot) for ~boil{10%min}, spread flat and left alone.

Simmer @&(~1)paella{} low with @large shrimp{1%lb}(450 g; shell on), @lemon{1}(cut in wedges) laid on top for ~simmer{8%min}.

Rest @&(~1)pan{} off the heat under a clean towel for ~rest{10%min}.

The crust on the bottom is the point and it is the one thing a table cannot hand you: it comes from a pan that is hotter at the edges than the middle, and only your own burner knows that. Listen for it in the last two minutes — a faint crackle, not a smell of burning — and pull the pan when you hear it.
